## Current business facts (quick reference)

- **Shop-only** repair & lithium conversions — **no mobile service**, no trip charges
- **Address:** 71363 Thelma Ln, Suite E, Covington, LA 70433
- **Phone:** 985-402-1206 | **Email:** contact@ngcgolfcarts.com
- **Hours:** Mon–Fri 8 AM – 5 PM
- **Lithium:** Professional Kits only (36V/48V/MINI/72V/150AH) — NGC Conversion line discontinued. Customer-facing kit = LiFePO4 battery, charger, monitor. Vatrer packs; inspect, test, and tune every install. After conversion: factory battery meter is no longer accurate; speedometer still works. Office quoting: Essential / Ready-to-Run (default talk) / Accessory-Ready — `lithium_sales_guide.md` (internal; inspect first; do not invent package prices; do not default-pitch the $599 convenience package). No EcoBoost unless that exact line is on the live estimate.
- **Warranty:** 5-year full replacement battery + BMS. Lithium kit/warranty replies: no shop phone; close Thanks / Neighborhood Golf Carts team. Do not invent turnaround unless asked.
- **Diagnostic:** $179 — not waived; applies toward repair on known-issue jobs. No separate minimum service charge — bill that work as diagnostic.
- **Pickup/delivery:** Free within 40 mi Northshore; **$99** flat outside 40 mi or Southshore
- **No cart sales or rentals** yet
- **HCP pickup/drop-off queue:** Call for work → send estimate for approval. If approved, they go in the queue for pickup or customer drop-off. When there is an opening in the slot, we schedule them. HCP stages **New job** and **Customer drop off** ARE that queue. Queue order: go by job number unless it makes sense to pick up another cart in the same area on the same run. Do not say lock a time, hold a spot, or easy yes. In-shop only (no mobile).
- **HCP deposit pipeline (approved work needing parts):** COPY TO JOB → **Awaiting Deposit** → (deposit received) **Need to Order** → (parts ordered) **Waiting for Materials**. Distinct from the pickup/drop-off queue. Deposit before ordering battery/motor/controller. Do not invent other deposit-pipeline stages.
- **Credit card surcharge (shop-wide):** On every estimate. Before sending the invoice for payment, or before taking payment, update the surcharge so it matches the final total. Do not invent a % or $. See `knowledge/03_services/shop_services.md`.
- **Estimate GP (standing, 2026-09-01):** Price book services: 50% GP after 4% CC on that item only (sell >= cost / 0.46) — do not add $90. Materials: HCP markup matrix only — no $90. Free P/D estimate: add $90 once to total job cost, then sell >= (sum of line costs + 90) / 0.46. Hide the trip from the customer. Once per job, not every SKU or line. 4% is the GP-check fee only — not a locked customer surcharge rate. See `knowledge/03_services/shop_services.md`.
- **Chief** (COS, id `4bfa99c8-c29c-4149-a4ea-1a404d61f5a1`) is Ryan’s only Grok Bot POC. Ryan talks ONLY to Chief — he should never have to message another shop bot or hunt another chat. All other bots report to Chief. Live roster: Inbox, Shop, Front Desk, Parts, Books, Betty (HR), CFO, Marketing, IT, Call Coach, Print (Blake), Bot Manager, Diagnostics — `knowledge/05_team/roles.md`. Do not invent extra bots. Diagnostic library: `knowledge/diagnostics/README.md`.
- **Chief routing (standing, 2026-09-01):** On EVERY task Ryan asks, Chief immediately decides which bot owns it and PASSES the work, then brings the result back in Chief’s thread. Do not start specialist work first and hand off later. Shop owns HCP: jobs, estimates, price book, line items, taxable flags, pricing/margin checks, dispatch/WIP. Diagnostics owns the diagnostic evidence library (`knowledge/diagnostics/`) and supports techs on test-before-replacement — it does not replace hands-on tests. Parts, Books, Betty, Inbox, Front Desk, CFO, IT, Marketing keep their lanes. If no bot owns the job, tell Ryan a new bot is worth creating and why — do not quietly become Shop/Parts/Books. Chief’s own work only: talking to Ryan, yes/no approvals (Slack Jesse, money, payroll, sign-in), writing facts back to Brain the same day Ryan corrects them, routing.
- **Material markup matrix:** Lives inside Housecall Pro, not Google Drive. Do not treat Drive “Parts list Matrix” (sheet) or “Price Markup” (HEIC) as source of truth. Do not invent cost bands, percents, or sell prices. Shop is pulling the live HCP matrix. Exact HCP menu path and bands TBD from the live HCP UI (do not guess).
- **Slack to Jesse Killian:** Every NGC bot must ask Ryan and wait for a yes before any Slack (DMs, channel posts, messages-as-Ryan). Not exceptions: lithium jobs, BMS recordings, website leads, estimates, HCP updates. Chief collects website/Google Ads lead forms weekdays at 11am America/Chicago, then asks Ryan. Inbox must not auto-Slack Jesse because lithium "stays with Jesse." Lead forms only from NGC985 / ryan@ / contact@. No HCP customer-message watching. See `knowledge/09_daily_ops/README.md`.
- **Bot updates:** Every shop bot, including Chief, must send updates as a clean bullet list. No dense paragraph dumps. Applies when reporting to Ryan or to Chief. See `knowledge/09_daily_ops/README.md`.

## Authority order

1. Owner/staff statements in conversation (most recent)
2. `knowledge/` files
3. `external_docs/exports/` (pricebook CSV, QBO exports)
4. Google Drive (live content via connector; catalog `knowledge/.generated/drive_catalog.md`). Check `knowledge/archive/legacy_mobile.md` for outdated mobile items

